li:InsuranceContract a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Insurance Product Offered"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A formal agreement providing coverage under specified terms and conditions. Induced from a Hierarchy placement via graph-native parent (entity role co-occurrence): subClassOf POLICY; cluster of 4 surface variant(s) merge…"@en,
        "A loan reduces the cash surrender value of a policy. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms loans reduce cash surrender value via deduction. The property links the policy to a deduction mechanis…"@en,
        "COI rates are guaranteed not to change. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence states that COI rates are guaranteed and not subject to increase, which aligns with the concept of a rate cap condition. The…"@en,
        "Contestability limited to initial policy period. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms that contestability applies only within a defined initial period (e.g., 2 years). The property links Insur…"@en,
        "Eligibility for coverage after employment termination. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence states that employees may port their coverage as an individual policy after leaving employment, indicating co…"@en,
        "Ensures minimum coverage value during policy decline. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows a floor ensures 0% interest when the index declines by 5%, which is quantified as a percentage. The prop…"@en,
        "Future children are automatically covered under the policy. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The policy automatically extends coverage to future children, indicating the existence of a coverage instance. The pr…"@en,
        "Limits maximum coverage amount under specified conditions. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows a single maximum coverage limit per policy, with examples like $1M cap. The property 'hasCoverageLi…"@en,
        "Policyholder must apply for portability before a deadline. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence specifies a time limit (31 days) for portability application, indicating a temporal constraint. The prope…"@en,
        "Policyholder must meet criteria to qualify for a split option. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The sentences indicate conditions (survival of both insureds, evidence of insurability) for exercising the split o…"@en,
        "Surrender charge applies within first 12 years. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms a surrender charge is applied within the first 12 years, and the charge is quantified as a monetary value.…"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
            owl:onProperty li:hasCoverageLimit ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
